            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0264" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.105A/6f: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-09T22:00:00-04:00">September 9,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>238. There is pending in Congress a bill to permit American Army and Navy
                    officers to serve under any foreign government whose defense is considered
                    essential to that of the United States. Upon enactment of the bill it is
                    contemplated that Colonel Schwarzkopf and his assistants, Colonel Boone and
                    Captain Preston, will enter into the service of the Iranian Government rather
                    than continue to act in their present advisory capacity. At that time it will be
                    necessary to draw up a contract for their services between the American and
                    Iranian Governments. A draft of such agreement will be transmitted to the
                    Legation for the Legation’s and Colonel Schwarzkopf’s suggestions for
                    alterations or additions to meet special conditions in Iran.</p>
                <p>Please advise Colonel Schwarzkopf of this procedure because at the time of his
                    departure he was under the impression that his contract would be made directly
                    between him and the Iranian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
